# Pokémon Eclipse / Asterra v0.2
# Native FireRed starter-lab integration plan
#
# This is intentionally a source-integration specification rather than a
# blind binary patch. Apply it to a compatible pret/pokefirered checkout after
# the source tree is present in the Asterra repository.
#
# Upstream reference:
# data/maps/PalletTown_ProfessorOaksLab/scripts.inc
#
# Current vanilla scene starts at:
# PalletTown_ProfessorOaksLab_ChooseStarterScene
#
# Existing upstream state variables:
# VAR_TEMP_1 = player starter selection
# VAR_TEMP_2 = battle position
# VAR_TEMP_3 = rival starter species
# VAR_TEMP_4 = rival starter trainer id
#
# Asterra will replace the opening choice scene with:
#
#   Lyra introduction
#       -> generation selection (I/II/III)
#       -> starter selection (3 choices)
#       -> store generation + choice
#       -> give selected species at Lv5
#       -> choose Nova counter
#       -> continue into the existing rival-battle scene
#
# Required new persistent variables should be allocated from the project's
# free permanent variable range rather than TEMP_VARS, because TEMP_VARS are
# cleared on map load.
#
# Required script state:
#   ASTERRA_STARTER_GENERATION
#   ASTERRA_STARTER_CHOICE
#   ASTERRA_NOVA_STARTER
#
# Required native game operations:
#   - native list/menu UI for generation selection
#   - native list/menu UI for starter selection
#   - party insertion using FireRed's existing GiveMon/givemon mechanism
#   - trainer selection using FireRed's trainer-battle system
#
# Nine initial choices:
#   Gen I:   BULBASAUR / CHARMANDER / SQUIRTLE
#   Gen II:  CHIKORITA / CYNDAQUIL / TOTODILE
#   Gen III: TREECKO / TORCHIC / MUDKIP
#
# Nova counter mapping:
#   choice 0 -> choice 2
#   choice 1 -> choice 0
#   choice 2 -> choice 1
#
# IMPORTANT:
# The current upstream lab script contains extensive movement choreography
# and fixed trainer battle labels. Those should be preserved where possible;
# only the starter-selection state and trainer selection need replacement.
#
# Do not replace the upstream file wholesale until the exact script-menu API
# and free save-variable allocation have been verified against the checkout.
